1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
A scanning machine is a virtual or physical machine that runs scans.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000
You can run scans on the same machine as the web server and enterprise server to begin with.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,000
When you follow the installation wizard, this is a default option that is selected.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Alternatively, you can set up as many external machines as you want and use them as dedicated scanning machines.

5
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:34,000
In this way, you can spread your scans across multiple scanning machines to avoid overloading a single machine.

6
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:39,000
You can assign a maximum number of current requests that can be run on each machine.

7
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Please refer to the system requirements section for more information about how many machines you might need to deploy.

8
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Note that if you decide to use external scanning machines, you need to authorize them in BurpSuite Enterprise Edition before you can use them to run scans.

9
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:03,000
On standard deployments, as opposed to Kubernetes deployments, scanning machines exist in one of several scanning pools.

10
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:10,000
These pools are used to manage the resources for different kinds of scans or for scanning different sorts of sites.

11
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:15,000
To assign the machine to a different pool, see Managing Scanning Pools.

12
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:16,000
